Heavy Periods During the First Two Days: Why Your Flow May Feel Stronger

For many women, the first couple of days of a period can be the heaviest. Managing increased menstrual flow during these days can be easier when you understand your cycle and choose suitable menstrual protection.

Why Are the First Days Often Heavier?

Menstrual flow can vary throughout the period. Some women experience heavier bleeding at the beginning, followed by lighter flow during the remaining days.

This variation means that the same sanitary pad may not always be suitable for every day of your cycle.

How Can You Prepare for Heavy Days?

Knowing your usual pattern is one of the simplest ways to prepare. If your first or second day is normally heavier, keep extra sanitary pads with you before your period begins.

Choose a pad with appropriate absorbency and coverage for your heavier days.

